*Relational Database (RDBMS) 
-Stores data in tables (rows & columns).
-Row = Record, Column = Attribute.
-Uses Primary Key to uniquely identify records.
-Uses Foreign Key to connect tables.
-Supports relationships between tables.
-Uses SQL to store and manage data.
-Reduces data redundancy.
-Ensures data integrity and consistency.

*SQL vs NoSQL Databases 
-SQL	NoSQL
-Relational database	Non-relational database
-Stores data in tables	Stores data as documents, key-value, graph, etc.
-Fixed schema	Flexible schema
-Uses SQL language	Uses different query methods
-Best for structured data	Best for unstructured/semi-structured data

*Basic SQL Syntax & Keywords 
-SELECT – Retrieve data
-FROM – Specify table
-WHERE – Filter records
-INSERT INTO – Add new record
-UPDATE – Modify existing data
-DELETE – Remove records
-CREATE TABLE – Create a table
-ALTER TABLE – Modify table structure
-DROP TABLE – Delete a table
-ORDER BY – Sort data
-GROUP BY – Group records
-HAVING – Filter grouped data
-DISTINCT – Remove duplicate values
-AS – Give an alias (temporary name)
-JOIN – Combine data from multiple tables

*Data Types in SQL (Short Key Points)
-Numeric Data Types
    -INT – Integer numbers
    -BIGINT – Large integers
    -DECIMAL – Exact decimal values
    -FLOAT – Approximate decimal values
-Character Data Types
    -CHAR – Fixed-length text
    -VARCHAR – Variable-length text
    -TEXT – Large text
-Date & Time Data Types
    DATE – Date only
    TIME – Time only
    DATETIME – Date and time
    TIMESTAMP – Date and time with automatic updates
    Boolean Data Type

*SQL Operators 
Arithmetic Operators
    + – Addition
    - – Subtraction
    * – Multiplication
    / – Division
    % – Modulus (Remainder)
Comparison Operators
    = – Equal to
    != / <> – Not equal to
    > – Greater than
    < – Less than
    >= – Greater than or equal to
    <= – Less than or equal to
Logical Operators
    AND – Both conditions true
    OR – Any one condition true
    NOT – Reverse the condition
Special Operators
    IN – Match multiple values
    BETWEEN – Range of values
    LIKE – Pattern matching
    IS NULL – Check NULL values

*Data Definition Language (DDL)
    CREATE – Create database/table
    ALTER – Modify table structure
    DROP – Delete database/table
    TRUNCATE – Remove all rows, keep table


*Data Manipulation Language (DML)
    INSERT – Add new records
    UPDATE – Modify existing records
    DELETE – Remove records